<title>USA: Mass to aid workers whose firms were shut by storm.</title>
<headline>Mass to aid workers whose firms were shut by storm.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts officials said workers who temporarily lost their jobs because their companies were damaged by the devastating Nor'easter two weeks ago will be eligible for special unemployment benefits.</p>
<p>The benefits will be available to any workers in the five eastern Massachusetts counties who were temporarily laid off because the storm, which dumped up to a foot of rain on the area, caused widespread flooding and millions of dollars in damage, the officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
